<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agnello Participazio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 827</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Agnello Particiaco</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agnello Participazio was Doge of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> from 811 to 827. Elected after the Frankish attack on the lagoon by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-of-italy">Pepin of Italy</a>, he moved the seat of government from Malamocco to the more defensible <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rialto">Rialto</a> islands, the core of the later city of Venice. He associated his sons with him in office, and the Participazio family supplied several doges in the ninth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/agnello-participazio.jpg" alt="Agnello Participazio" width="309" height="328" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Domenico Tintoretto · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Agnello_Participazio_(series_by_Domenico_Tintoretto_-_Doge%E2%80%99s_Palace).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
